1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,640
Welcome.

4
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:24,100
Oh my, this material is nice.

5
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:27,500
This one and this one, too.

6
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:35,210
What? When did he move?

7
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,880
Is this guy riding a city bike?

8
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,690
It is definitely somewhere nearby.

9
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,520
Where did he stop?

10
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,260
Is he moving again?

11
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,160
Is he making deliveries?

12
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,660
Why is he roaming around so much?

13
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,850
(Da Mi's Tablet)

14
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:32,800
(Da Mi's Tablet)

15
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,670
(Da Mi's Tablet)

16
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:42,170
Got you, you thief!

17
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:45,310
What are you doing?

18
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:48,680
You really were the one
who stole it.

19
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:50,350
What are you saying I stole?

20
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,450
Look.

21
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:56,290
No wonder you were following me...

22
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:58,020
from the bus stop,
pretending to know me.

23
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,230
Is there anything else you stole
besides my tablet?

24
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:06,900
It was not me, but my sister
who took it.

25
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:08,330
She said even the patterns matched.

26
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:11,600
Didn't you notice? How careless!

27
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:14,510
Your sister?

28
00:02:16,810 --> 00:02:18,140
Do you not know Cha Se Na?

29
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:20,350
She took it out in front of you...

30
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:21,510
and brought back yours by mistake.

31
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:23,680
How did that...

32
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,290
Wait, she is your sister?

33
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,850
Then why not bring it to the store?

34
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:31,320
Why carry it around with you?

35
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:35,590
Well, I heard personal meetings
with customers are prohibited.

36
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:37,300
Since it is not work-related,

37
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,030
I intentionally did not go see you,
Kang Da Mi.

38
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,400
Fine. Whatever you say, sir.

39
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,040
I will be going now.

40
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:46,070
Excuse me, wait a minute.

41
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:48,240
Anyway.

42
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:50,810
Why do you not review the designs
on your tablet one more time?

43
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:54,050
Why are you looking through
someone else's...

44
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:06,990
What is the problem?

45
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:10,760
Do you really not know?

46
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:15,930
Well, if you just tell me
to review it,

47
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,040
how am I supposed to...

48
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:19,340
Look.

49
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:23,140
First, this part is problematic.

50
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,240
You are using this fabric
for the bottoms?

51
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:28,410
If you apply this material
directly to the clothes,

52
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:30,750
it will be so heavy that no one
will wear it.

53
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:33,920
Your design does not consider
practicality at all.

54
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:36,820
Can you even call something clothes
if people cannot wear it?

55
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,090
Can you?

56
00:03:41,590 --> 00:03:42,830
Should we go over
the other ones, too?

57
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:45,600
This fabric here. Look next to it.

58
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,530
This fabric has
such poor elasticity...

59
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,640
that if you commercialize
this design right away,

60
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,240
it will definitely
cause problems later.

61
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,370
This part of the design is too thin,

62
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:55,970
so it will not be easy
to manufacture.

63
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:01,380
So what is the alternative?

64
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:03,750
Why should I be the one
to tell you that?

65
00:04:04,650 --> 00:04:05,950
You do not even have an alternative,

66
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:07,520
but you are just nitpicking
every little thing.

67
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:08,920
Who says I have no alternative?

68
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:11,960
Then tell me what it is.

69
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:17,000
Have you ever visited a flea market?

70
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,230
A flea market?

71
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,400
Someone who wants
to be a designer...

72
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,870
has never even been to one.

73
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,340
That is truly unbelievable.
Unbelievable.

74
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:29,440
Who said I have not been there?
I have.

75
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,710
You have?

76
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:35,050
You take the bus, right, Kang Da Mi?

77
00:04:35,450 --> 00:04:37,520
You do not seem like
you drive your own car.

78
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:39,050
When you go to the flea market,

79
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,150
which exit do you take?

80
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,720
- Excuse me?
- The subway is usually faster.

81
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,060
Or maybe not? Do you take the bus?

82
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:47,760
Which bus number do you take?

83
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:50,300
Well...

84
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,360
Even if not the flea market,

85
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:54,870
you go to Dongdaemun Market
often, right?

86
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:56,530
And sometimes Namdaemun, too.

87
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,970
That is right.
That is definitely right.

88
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:00,770
That is definitely right?

89
00:05:01,110 --> 00:05:03,610
You've never been to a flea market?

90
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,750
I surrender.

91
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:10,920
I was wrong. I lied.

92
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:18,560
Come to Unjeong Station
by two tomorrow afternoon...

93
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:19,620
and take exit three.

94
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:21,730
If you are even one minute late,

95
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:22,990
we will never see each other again.

96
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:26,200
- Got it?
- I have work tomorrow.

97
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:30,370
- My day off is...
- That's your problem.

98
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:31,940
It is none of my business.

99
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:37,640
What is this? It is confusing.
I almost took it again.

100
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,550
Money tree.

101
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:54,930
Gosh, what is wrong with him?
He only says what he wants to say.

102
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:56,830
He is such a show-off.

103
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:08,640
Kim Pro, you crazy...

104
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:11,940
I thought you only stole my money,
but what have you been doing?

105
00:06:14,150 --> 00:06:15,150
Wait a minute.

106
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,220
Increase this quarter's orders
from Uijeong Trading...

107
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:19,350
by 30 percent this quarter.

108
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,150
What? That much all of a sudden?

109
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:24,020
Why? Is there a problem?

110
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:26,990
No. It is not exactly a problem...

111
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,460
Seriously?

112
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:31,100
I am the one in charge.
Why do you keep asking questions?

113
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:33,970
I only thought that if the orders...

114
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:36,900
- increase too sharply...
- Want to take charge instead?

115
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:40,470
No, what are you talking about...

116
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:43,370
Then proceed with it.

117
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,240
Yes, understood.

118
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:49,150
Right, now I get it.

119
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:52,250
It was strange how
the Uijeong Trading orders...

120
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,650
were always issued verbally.

121
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,490
I got played. I really got played.

122
00:07:04,930 --> 00:07:06,860
I got played beautifully.

123
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:23,680
Se Na, do you truly want
to start your own business?

124
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:27,690
Yes, Grandma.
Yes, Grandma. What is the occasion?

125
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:31,290
- What's going on?
- Even I can tell...

126
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:33,720
studying just isn't for you.

127
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:37,160
You are right. I gave up on that
in the fourth grade.

128
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,100
Well, if you really want
to start a business...

129
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,970
Here, look at this.

130
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:47,170
What is this?

131
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:50,440
They owe your father's company...

132
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:52,040
over 100,000 dollars each.

133
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,280
I've picked out a few of them.

134
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:58,020
I'll give you six months.
From the people on this list...

135
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:00,120
collect a debt from at least one.

136
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:03,150
If you do,
I will fund your business.

137
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:06,160
What? That is ridiculous.

138
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:10,530
You want me to go collect debts?
From complete strangers?

139
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:11,860
That is...

140
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:16,830
money from your father's company.
It is my money.

141
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:18,200
Which means
it is our family's money.

142
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:24,440
They borrowed our money
and keep putting off paying it back.

143
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,850
Let us see how much you can collect.

144
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:32,250
I want to see if you have
what it takes to be a manager.

145
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:36,250
- Our Se Na is in trouble.
- Yes.

146
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,760
Right, ma'am?

147
00:08:41,490 --> 00:08:42,590
What should I do?

148
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:45,430
This is a huge problem.

149
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:47,530
But...

150
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:51,140
you can't fix trouble
until it actually happens.

151
00:08:51,370 --> 00:08:53,970
You have nothing to lose,
so just try it.

152
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,840
It is not like she is asking you
to print money out of thin air.

153
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:03,350
I will do it.
I will give it a try, Grandma.

154
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:07,950
Really? That is the spirit.
That is my granddaughter.

155
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,660
This will be fun to watch.

156
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:14,160
Good.

157
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:15,990
Come this way.

158
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:17,960
Right this way.

159
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:22,430
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

160
00:09:22,570 --> 00:09:26,040
The area's bustling,
and rent's been low for ten years,

161
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:28,170
and nothing inside needs repairs.

162
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:31,940
You just need to bring in
your equipment and put up a sign.

163
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,110
Is this the commercial space
you mentioned?

164
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:37,580
Right across from the soup shop...

165
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,620
right across from
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.

166
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:45,060
Yes. Is there something
you do not like?

167
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:48,460
This chicken soup restaurant
has a ton of regulars.

168
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:51,360
They get countless franchise offers,
and they are constantly asked...

169
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:54,370
to be featured on food shows,
but they turn them all down.

170
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:58,340
The owner and her mother-in-law
know exactly what they want,

171
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,470
so they just run their own place.

172
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:03,870
They built their success today
just by serving their regulars.

173
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:08,110
Even if you only get their customers
as your patients.

174
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:10,250
I guarantee...

175
00:10:10,510 --> 00:10:12,280
you will be able
to buy this building...

176
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,950
under your name within five years.

177
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,790
Shall we go inside and take a look?

178
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:21,060
I will sign the contract.

179
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:25,930
Excuse me? You have not even
seen the property yet.

180
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,970
You said that within five years,
I'd have enough money...

181
00:10:29,030 --> 00:10:30,270
to buy this building in my name.

182
00:10:30,770 --> 00:10:31,770
I will sign the contract.

183
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:37,810
Mi Mi.

184
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:41,280
Are you paying the price
for raising your sons poorly...

185
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:44,650
by keeping your mouth shut all day
in front of your mother-in-law?

186
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:48,020
What is there for me to say?

187
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,420
Then I should've stopped eating...

188
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,890
and died long ago...

189
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,730
since I am the mother
of the most terrible son in the world.

190
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:57,900
Oh, Mother.

191
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:01,230
Ms. Jo!

192
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,900
It is leased.
The commercial space is leased.

193
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,970
It is leased?
Who said they are moving in?

194
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:12,080
It seems it is finally leased.
That is great.

195
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,580
It caused so much trouble
being vacant.

196
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:16,250
- Right, Mrs. Choi?
- Yes, yes.

197
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:19,650
But who is moving in?

198
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:23,790
(Always Together Realty)

199
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:25,790
Yes.

200
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:29,430
I've seen a deal this quick...

201
00:11:29,530 --> 00:11:32,400
and completely trouble-free...

202
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:35,230
fewer than ten times...

203
00:11:35,370 --> 00:11:37,840
in all my years as a realtor.

204
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:42,010
I stamped the seal because you said
you were in a hurry,

205
00:11:42,170 --> 00:11:44,440
but how could you not even take
a look inside the commercial space?

206
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:45,940
This is quite surprising.

207
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,410
When are you opening your clinic?

208
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:52,380
As soon as I hire a receptionist,
I plan to open right away.

209
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:54,790
I see.

210
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:58,160
If by any chance,
while you are preparing to open,

211
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,290
you find any issues
inside the space...

212
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:03,160
Yes, I will contact you right away.

213
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:05,360
Yes, please do.

214
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,210
- Oh my.
- My gosh.

215
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:24,950
- Are you okay, Ms. Jo?
- Were you burned anywhere?

216
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:27,320
I am fine. The coffee
had cooled down enough.

217
00:12:27,650 --> 00:12:29,720
- The tissues...
- Right.

218
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:33,090
Please wipe it with this.

219
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:36,990
Right...

220
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,260
Thank you.

221
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:47,610
I have other matters to attend to,
so I will be going now.

222
00:12:47,870 --> 00:12:52,080
Okay. But this...

223
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:54,380
You can give it back to me later.

224
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:56,080
Please do not worry
too much about it.

225
00:12:58,050 --> 00:13:01,550
- Okay.
- You made a great deal, sir.

226
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,820
You will fall asleep
counting your money.

227
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,360
Yes.

228
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,690
- Goodbye.
- Yes, goodbye.

229
00:13:14,770 --> 00:13:18,770
That happened in a flash!

230
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:21,710
It feels like pulling out
an aching tooth.

231
00:13:21,770 --> 00:13:24,380
It was strange that it was vacant
for so long anyway.

232
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,140
You are treating me to seaweed soup
at the sauna, right?

233
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:30,650
Of course. Thank you.

234
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:35,250
He is so incredibly sweet.

235
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,690
But who would believe
he is a doctor?

236
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:39,320
Does he not just look like
a free spirit?

237
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,330
What is the word? A bohemian, right?

238
00:13:43,690 --> 00:13:45,930
Wait, you said he comes
to your restaurant often?

239
00:13:46,330 --> 00:13:48,030
Once in a while,
when I almost forget about him.

240
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,870
I only found out
he was a doctor this time too.

241
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:54,170
You should try to make
a move on him.

242
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:57,040
- What are you talking about?
- Why are you playing coy?

243
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:59,210
Have we been in this business
for just a day or two?

244
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:01,510
You can tell just by looking at him
that he is single.

245
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,180
What does him being single
have to do with me?

246
00:14:05,850 --> 00:14:08,050
- I'm leaving.
- Wait, honey.

247
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:12,020
I did not notice earlier,
but why do you look so gloomy?

248
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:14,290
By any chance...

249
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:16,030
Do you know something?

250
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:18,330
Know what?

251
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,360
I mean...

252
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,870
I was wondering if you heard
any news about the kids' father.

253
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,400
Did he die?

254
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:26,370
What? No.

255
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:28,940
Unless it is news
that he died somewhere,

256
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:30,870
do not even bring him up to me.

257
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:34,610
Even without him,
my life right now is barely a life.

258
00:14:43,850 --> 00:14:44,860
I am home.

259
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,690
It's a money tree.

260
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:51,660
- Did you buy it yourself?
- Yes.

261
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,460
It caught my eye
as I was walking by.

262
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:55,300
I'll put it in Grandma's room.

263
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,670
- It is pretty, right?
- Yes.

264
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:58,800
Is she in her room?

265
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:00,300
Yes.

266
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:03,440
She's been asking for you,
Seung Yun.

267
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:04,910
Is that so?

268
00:15:05,410 --> 00:15:07,180
Then you should have called me
right away.

269
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:08,610
Well...

270
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:10,510
She is not thinking clearly.

271
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:17,760
Grandma.

272
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:20,490
I am here.

273
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:22,190
It is Seung Yun.

274
00:15:28,130 --> 00:15:30,130
Grandma, what is all of this?

275
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Yes.

276
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:33,740
Hello.

277
00:15:35,110 --> 00:15:37,810
Yes, well, everything
is sold out today.

278
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:39,410
I am closing up shop.

279
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,180
But...

280
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:44,550
these are not for sale.

281
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:47,050
My Jun Sung.

282
00:15:47,650 --> 00:15:51,660
My oldest son wore these shoes.

283
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,660
Go away. I cannot sell them.

284
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,530
These are not for sale.

285
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,160
Go away.

286
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:05,970
Are these the shoes
your oldest son used to wear?

287
00:16:07,170 --> 00:16:09,510
How do you have so many?

288
00:16:10,910 --> 00:16:13,180
How did you keep them for so long?

289
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:16,250
These are the shoes my dad...

290
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:20,150
I guess these are the shoes
my father used to wear, Grandma.

291
00:16:21,350 --> 00:16:22,350
Yes.

292
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:26,620
You see, I had no money.

293
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,130
My Jun Sung...

294
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:31,530
When the other children
wore rubber shoes...

295
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,030
and walked through the alleys,

296
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:37,230
only my Jun Sung
went out to play barefoot.

297
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,040
One day,

298
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:42,570
I was cleaning
a building's toilet...

299
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:47,610
and picked up discarded
cabbage leaves in an alley.

300
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:50,810
I wanted to make him some porridge
with soybean paste broth.

301
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,950
But then my little boy...

302
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:56,720
cut his foot on broken glass...

303
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:59,120
and was bleeding terribly.

304
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:01,060
He was groaning in pain...

305
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:04,730
but didn't want to alarm his mom...

306
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:07,100
so he could barely cry.

307
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,130
I...

308
00:17:10,670 --> 00:17:12,700
saw poverty as my absolute enemy.

309
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:16,910
The poverty that made my son
grow up far too quickly...

310
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:20,880
felt like my worst enemy.

311
00:17:22,010 --> 00:17:23,650
So, at that moment,

312
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:27,320
I just gritted my teeth
and started making money.

313
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,590
Grandma.

314
00:17:31,890 --> 00:17:32,890
Grandma.

315
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:38,600
Once I finally settled...

316
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:40,500
my bitter score with poverty,

317
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,800
fate itself...

318
00:17:43,570 --> 00:17:45,340
took my son away from me.

319
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,070
You hear me?

320
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,310
My son, Jun Sung.

321
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:53,510
They took my son...

322
00:17:54,450 --> 00:17:57,450
away from me is what I am saying.

323
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,450
Grandma.

324
00:18:04,190 --> 00:18:07,320
That is not your fault.
You need to know that, okay?

325
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,290
Grandma, please look at me.

326
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,530
I'm your eldest grandson, Seung Yun.

327
00:18:12,930 --> 00:18:14,400
I'm the bloodline your eldest son,
Jun Sung, left behind.

328
00:18:14,470 --> 00:18:16,870
I'm Seung Yun, Grandma.

329
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,770
Grandma, why are you acting
like this?

330
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,540
Grandma,

331
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:23,870
why are you really doing this?

332
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,780
Grandma, look at me
straight in the eyes, okay?

333
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,410
That is pretty.

334
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:32,680
Isn't that a money tree?

335
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:35,850
- Right?
- Yes, do you like it?

336
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,790
- Yes.
- Would you like to try raising it?

337
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,060
No.

338
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:42,690
People have known for ages...

339
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:44,500
that a money tree rarely blooms.

340
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:47,160
I am not confident.

341
00:18:47,930 --> 00:18:48,930
Yes.

342
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,240
Money trees rarely bloom.

343
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:53,840
So on the day it blooms,

344
00:18:54,470 --> 00:18:56,710
people see it as a very
special sign.

345
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:57,980
Prosperity,

346
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:01,580
flourishing, wealth, and riches.

347
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:03,910
People usually know it
to mean things like that.

348
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:05,720
But Grandma, a money tree...

349
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:08,350
- Yes.
- It means good luck.

350
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,920
- Good luck.
- Yes.

351
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:12,660
It means a fresh start.

352
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:14,560
Oh, right.

353
00:19:15,330 --> 00:19:16,360
That is right.

354
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:18,130
Good luck.

355
00:19:19,130 --> 00:19:21,800
- A fresh start.
- So, Grandma.

356
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:24,030
Grandma,

357
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:26,670
please stay healthy
for a long, long time...

358
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:28,610
and always stay by my side
just like now.

359
00:19:29,570 --> 00:19:32,080
We should see this
money tree bloom...

360
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:33,610
together, don't you think?

361
00:19:35,010 --> 00:19:36,010
Right?

362
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:45,090
Seung Yun.
My precious eldest grandson.

363
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:50,060
Please understand your grandma,
even if I must do this to you.

364
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,500
For the rest of my days, I intend...

365
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:56,630
to be your shield.

366
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:04,370
Okay.

367
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:34,240
My baby.

368
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:36,370
Su Ah.

369
00:20:42,510 --> 00:20:47,120
- Was the school lunch good?
- School lunch is always the same.

370
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:51,660
What did you play today?

371
00:20:53,290 --> 00:20:57,060
I played with blocks
and did some origami...

372
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,560
and jumped rope.

373
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,960
It is always the same.

374
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,600
Nothing special happened?

375
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:06,140
You are the one
with special things happening, Dad.

376
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,570
How will you pay 600 dollars...

377
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:12,910
in monthly expenses, starting now?
Why aren't you working, Dad?

378
00:21:14,950 --> 00:21:16,050
Hey, daughter.

379
00:21:16,550 --> 00:21:19,120
That is not something
a kid like you should worry about.

380
00:21:19,450 --> 00:21:22,450
I will take care of my own business.

381
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:26,320
- Do you not trust your Dad?
- No, I do not.

382
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:30,390
Then trust me.

383
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:33,800
At least my daughter
should trust me, kiddo.

384
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:53,820
Su Ah, I am going to the restroom,

385
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:56,220
- so wait here a bit.
- Okay.

386
00:22:04,190 --> 00:22:06,530
- Where is the restroom here?
- The restroom?

387
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,620
Knock, knock.

388
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:34,220
Who is it?

389
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:36,530
It's Su Ah's mom.

390
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:39,000
Liar.

391
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:41,770
Wait, what? It is true.

392
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:46,140
My turn. Knock, knock.

393
00:22:47,970 --> 00:22:49,270
Who is it?

394
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:51,370
I am Kang Su Ah.

395
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,710
Who is Kang Su Ah...

396
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:56,910
again?

397
00:22:57,210 --> 00:22:58,250
Kim Mi Seon.

398
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:01,120
I am Kim Mi Seon's daughter,
Kang Su Ah.

399
00:23:02,250 --> 00:23:05,020
Ding-dong, you are correct.

400
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:07,060
- Mom.
- That is right, my daughter.

401
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,130
Mom.

402
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:14,200
What is going on
with my baby's hair?

403
00:23:14,530 --> 00:23:16,900
Your teacher was so busy, right?

404
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:18,070
Yes.

405
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:21,470
My friends were fighting
and hurting each other.

406
00:23:21,910 --> 00:23:23,570
Even their moms came.

407
00:23:23,910 --> 00:23:24,980
Is that right?

408
00:23:25,540 --> 00:23:29,310
So your teacher did not have time
to fix your hair?

409
00:23:29,810 --> 00:23:30,810
Yes.

410
00:23:31,850 --> 00:23:35,020
Mom, being a teacher
is a really hard job.

411
00:23:36,050 --> 00:23:38,360
By the way, did you eat, Mom?

412
00:24:01,650 --> 00:24:03,780
(Please return it after use.)

413
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:12,920
Just my luck.

414
00:24:13,860 --> 00:24:16,330
A basement rental at my age?
How did it come to this?

415
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:22,070
Well, even if I am in this state,

416
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:25,400
I must marry Ye Ri
into the Hwanggeum family.

417
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:28,470
I need to look for a job right now.

418
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:30,340
(Part-Time Fairy)

419
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:31,640
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine Desk)

420
00:24:31,710 --> 00:24:32,940
(Hiring Nursing Assistant)

421
00:24:35,550 --> 00:24:37,150
Internal medicine desk staff?

422
00:24:37,750 --> 00:24:38,980
It is close to home,

423
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:41,180
and they do not care
about age or experience.

424
00:24:41,420 --> 00:24:43,620
The desk and nursing assistant job...

425
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:45,320
requires nursing assistant certification.

426
00:24:45,390 --> 00:24:47,020
Oh, my.

427
00:24:47,090 --> 00:24:49,390
This job is absolutely
perfect for me.

428
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:52,160
My nursing assistant certificate...

429
00:24:52,230 --> 00:24:53,460
and the training I kept up with...

430
00:24:53,530 --> 00:24:56,370
are finally paying off.
I was right to stay prepared.

431
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:59,170
I should apply right away
before someone else takes it.

432
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:01,270
(Mobile Application,
Application Complete)

433
00:25:04,170 --> 00:25:05,180
What is this?

434
00:25:05,810 --> 00:25:07,780
"Can you come for an interview
tomorrow at two o'clock?"

435
00:25:08,850 --> 00:25:10,880
Yes, I am available.

436
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:18,760
As the kids say these days,

437
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:20,790
I have the perfect face
to pass any interview.

438
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:25,860
Welcome, hello.
Goodbye, please come again.

439
00:25:26,530 --> 00:25:28,060
You're laughing so hard...

440
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:30,070
you didn't see me come in?

441
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:32,140
You are home? Did you eat?

442
00:25:32,770 --> 00:25:34,140
Did you eat something bad?

443
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:37,070
Why are you suddenly asking
about my meals and scaring me?

444
00:25:37,070 --> 00:25:38,740
I did not eat anything bad.

445
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:42,280
I just feel like I am flying
for the first time in a while.

446
00:25:42,550 --> 00:25:46,520
It feels like the road ahead
is lined with flowers again.

447
00:25:47,980 --> 00:25:48,990
A flower-lined road?

448
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:51,250
Yes, a flower-lined road.

449
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,770
Hello, Team Leader Cha.
Good morning.

450
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:04,870
Yes, morning.

451
00:26:20,980 --> 00:26:22,920
Let me ask you something,
Assistant Manager Kang.

452
00:26:23,650 --> 00:26:26,560
I ignored him,
and he spoke right up.

453
00:26:28,290 --> 00:26:30,890
Yes, Team Leader Cha,
what are you curious about?

454
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:34,160
Assistant Manager Kang, have you
worn sneakers with a skirt...

455
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:35,730
and run as fast as you could?

456
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:37,630
Sneakers?

457
00:26:42,110 --> 00:26:45,740
- Are you taking that to Mother?
- Yes, the housekeeper said...

458
00:26:45,810 --> 00:26:47,780
she woke up early this morning.

459
00:26:48,210 --> 00:26:49,510
Let us go greet her together, then.

460
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,640
- Mother.
- Yes?

461
00:27:20,140 --> 00:27:21,140
Mother.

462
00:27:22,350 --> 00:27:23,410
Mother.

463
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:25,550
What are you hiding there?

464
00:27:26,580 --> 00:27:27,580
Hiding what?

465
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:29,790
That.

466
00:27:30,050 --> 00:27:33,360
What is in that black plastic bag
you are holding?

467
00:27:33,790 --> 00:27:35,330
What? This...

468
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:37,360
This?

469
00:27:39,660 --> 00:27:40,960
Leave, all of you!

470
00:27:41,300 --> 00:27:42,300
Mother...

471
00:27:43,800 --> 00:27:45,200
I said leave!

472
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:08,660
(Mission: Mompossible)

473
00:28:08,790 --> 00:28:11,190
His name is Dae Chi?
You're my ticket to a business!

474
00:28:12,630 --> 00:28:15,270
- Seriously!
- Hey, you have to go to work.

475
00:28:15,470 --> 00:28:19,900
The fact that my son called you
all the way to the company to meet...

476
00:28:20,170 --> 00:28:23,370
is proof that he has started
to suspect you.

477
00:28:23,740 --> 00:28:27,180
But Seung Yun,
if you live your life freely...

478
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:30,510
Is Grandma just a duty
and a burden to you two?

479
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:33,120
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
